.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murk-agent-connect 1  "connect " 
.SH NAME
murk\-agent\-connect \- Add `murk mcp` to an AI client\*(Aqs MCP config and mint a scoped grant for it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurk agent connect\fR [\fB\-\-allow\-tag\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-only\fR> [\fICLIENT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add `murk mcp` to an AI client\*(Aqs MCP config and mint a scoped grant for it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<ONLY>\fR
Keys the agent may read (required — fails closed)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-tag\fR \fI<ALLOW_TAG>\fR
Set the agent allow\-list to these tags before granting (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-exec\fR
Also enable the `murk_exec` tool in the MCP server (writes `\-\-allow\-exec` into the client config)
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR [default: 2h]
Grant time to live, e.g. 30m, 2h, 7d (reads fail closed after expiry)
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: mcp]
Grant name (used to disconnect/revoke it later)
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<VAULT>\fR [default: .murk]
Vault filename
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICLIENT\fR]
Client to configure: claude, cursor, vscode, zed, gemini, omp or codex. Omit it to configure every client that already has a config file or marker directory (such as `.cursor/`) next to the vault
